hogwarts legacy has been delayed to 2022  and i think there's a chance  avalanche ends up dropping support for  the ps4  and xbox one it's a question many of you  have been asking and in today's video  we'll break down that potential decision  and what i think is going to happen  people of the internet retro raconteur  here if we're meeting for the first time  i'm just the dad who loves games and the  stories they tell  we post videos every week here on  youtube and if you want to stay up to  date on all the latest hogwarts legacy  news theories and discussion then this  is the channel for you  despite a very rough year in 2020  hogwarts legacy fans always had  something to look forward to with the  game scheduled to release in 2021.  unfortunately those hopes were shattered  when avalanche and wb  announced the decision to delay the game  all the way to 2022  i've already made a couple of videos on  the subject but one of the questions  i've continued to see  over and over again is what this lengthy  delay could mean  for the ps4 and xbox one versions of the  game  now when hogwarts legacy was officially  unveiled back in september 2020 it was  confirmed to be in development for pc  ps4 ps5 xbox one and the xbox series  family of consoles  pretty much everything except the  nintendo switch gets in on the action  now to be completely clear as far as the  official word from avalanche and wb goes  we have heard absolutely nothing about  cancellation of old platforms if you go  to the website right now  at least at the time of recording this  video that is ps4  and xbox one are still in fact listed at  the bottom of the website along with the  others  now we know the game has been in  development since at least  2018 so it's safe to say they entered  this process planning for this to be a  ps4 and xbox one game  who knows how much behind the scenes  knowledge they had of ps5 and xbox  series x but we can be fairly confident  this game didn't start with those  systems at the forefront of their minds  when hogwarts legacy was originally  slated for 2021 releasing on  all these systems made perfect sense the  ps5 and xbox series x would have only  been out for one year and a very supply  constrained year at that  it made perfect financial sense to  release the games on both current gen  and last gen tech but now that it's set  for 2022 instead  should things change i put this question  out to you guys in one of our recent  videos and you all had a lot of great  arguments on both sides of this  i gotta say most of you were also super  respectful of one another in the  comments and i can't even begin to  describe how happy that makes me so  thank you all so much for that and  let's keep it going on this video as  well it's not too late to share your  thoughts on this if any of these  arguments i'm about to discuss  really resonate with you then be sure to  leave a comment and let me know how you  feel about all this so those who were  okay with the game dropping last gen  support most often cited the overall  quality of hogwarts legacy as their  primary concern  the theory here would be that without  having to worry about the older tech of  ps4 and xbox one  the devs could instead focus solely on  the more powerful hardware and thus do  even more great things within the game  itself  people on the other side argue that  dropping ps4 and xbox one support  wouldn't be fair to owners of those  consoles who haven't been able to  upgrade yet either due to supply  constraints or financial reasons  i mean we did have a very tough year due  to a worldwide pandemic  numerous people losing their jobs and  having less disposable income  so while the unique nature of 2020 makes  hogwarts legacy in somewhat of a  different position  it's definitely not the first time that  a game has been in a spot like this  it's a question that gets brought up  with each new console generation as devs  and publishers are faced with the  decision of how long they should  continue to support  old hardware let's take a look at some  of the heavy hitters such as madden and  call of duty you'll find they're  typically released on previous  generation hardware even  three years after the launch of new  systems just as one example the ps4  released in november of 2013.  now call of duty ghost was the first  game to release on both the ps3  and ps4 the ps3 and xbox 360 would  continue to get the brand new call of  duty game all the way up until 2016 with  call of duty infinite warfare which  released on  only ps4 xbox one and pc if you look at  the history of madden it follows a  similar pattern  but these are of course annual heavy  hitting titles that are sure  fire sales juggernauts what about brand  new titles  sure there are numerous examples out  there but i went straight to wb's  history to see what we could find  let's look at middle earth shadow of  mordor this released almost a full  year after the launch of the ps4 and  still came out on ps3  and xbox 360 as well as ps4 xbox one and  pc  2015's batman arkham knight however only  released on the newer ps4  xbox one and pc so when we look to  recent  video game history it would appear you  can make arguments in either direction  on this  i can certainly appreciate the arguments  on both sides of this i really can  however i don't personally believe it to  be an issue of  fairness as some folks were saying in  the comments wb and avalanche  are both companies that have to make  decisions in their best interest from a  financial standpoint as they also work  to maintain a healthy work environment  and strive to make the best game  possible  if they feel that keeping this game on  the older generation tech  is really going to hold it back then i  can totally understand a move to the  current gen only  i also saw a few arguments that fans  wouldn't want to buy a new system just  for one game  by 2022 though and maybe even late 2022  depending on when hogwarts legacy  actually does manage to release i'm not  so sure how valid that argument will  still be  i mean for me personally there are  already plenty of exclusive ps5 games  out now and scheduled for the rest of  2021 that i'm super excited about  of course that number is only going to  go up even further in 2022.  all that being said though i do think  it's in the best interest of wb  to keep the games on ps4 and xbox one  i'll explain why for me it really comes  down to two  important questions number one how much  are they being held back by the previous  generations tech  look make no mistake about it the ps4  and xbox one were fine systems in their  day with some pretty amazing open world  games however  they're both known for having incredibly  weak cpus frankly even when they first  released those were weak cpus  now in 2021 and especially in 2022 these  cpus will be practically ancient  the ps5 and xbox series x have far more  power and it could potentially make  avalanches job  much easier if they didn't have to worry  about support for the old generation  tech  would they be able to make a drastically  improved game by focusing solely on the  current gen systems  considering that development actually  started on ps4 and xbox one  i'm not so sure that's actually the case  and unfortunately that's really only a  question that  avalanche would be able to answer  truthfully the second big question to  consider is how many ps5s and xbox  series x's will be out in the wild by  mid to late 2022.  they certainly don't have any problem  selling but short supply and scalpers  continue to be a pretty massive problem  amd supplies key hardware components for  both ps5 and xbox series x and their ceo  doesn't expect supply to catch up with  demand until at least  the second half of 2021 okay so let's  just say they actually  are able to ramp up production heading  into 2022 and they can actually get out  more ps5s and xbox series x's  is that a gamble that hogwarts legacy  can take of  locking out ps4's absolutely massive 100  plus million install base  at the end of the day that gargantuan  install base combined with the supply  problems of current gen will ultimately  result in avalanche  keeping their commitment to both ps4 and  xbox one owners  at least that's what i believe if you  all enjoyed this discussion and want me  to keep making hogwarts legacy videos  then make sure to hit that like button  before you go  as always guys and gals thank you so  much for watching i'll talk to you again  soon
 

